  "body": "Why: our Sodick post writes the 1998 Mark 21 word set. A machine owner dry-ran our kit on a **Sodick AQ600L with an LN2W control** and reported that the Mark 21 naming does not fit his control. The public **Sodick LN1W/LN2W operation manual** (Sodick Inc., 2012; covers AQ400L/AQ600L) states the LN2W program format.\n\nWhat the LN2W manual states (summary; source for the clean-room record):\n- **Taper:** `G51` (left) / `G52` (right) with `A<angle per side>`, cancel `G50`; the taper starts during the move to the first surface and returns to vertical on the next XY move after `G50`. `TP` / `TN` load the Table-to-Program / Table-to-Next registers from the program. (Our post writes the Mark 21 `G74/G75` + `U V` form: wrong for LN2W.)\n- **Taper heights** are control settings: Table to Limit, Upper (follows Z), Lower, Program (worktable to part bottom), Next.\n- **Program start (manual example):** `G54 G90`, `G92 X0 Y0`, `G29` (reference point memory for the AWT) before `T91` (thread), `T84` (high flush), `C001`, `G41`/`G42 H001`; skim passes change `C` / `H` and use `T85` (low flush); end `M02`.\n- **T codes:** T82/T83 drain closed/open, T84/T85 high/low flush, T90 cut wire, T91 thread, T96/T97 fill pump on/off.\n- **Wire offset:** G40/G41/G42 with H registers per pass.\n\nOwner notes (2026-11-25, relayed): machine is an AQ600L, control LN2W; he wants `G0 Z0` at the top \"to bring the top head down\" - **held until he says what Z0 is on his setup** (the manual example has no Z move; the operator sets the nozzle-gap height), because a wrong Z move can hit the upper head.\n\nWhat is needed:\n1. A post dialect **\"Sodick LN2W\"** beside the Mark 21 one (the Mark 21 post stays for older controls): the start sequence above, G51/G52 A / G50 taper, TP/TN, H registers per pass, the T codes above.\n2. A machine file **Sodick AQ600L** (travels X/Y/Z/U/V and table/work limits from Sodick's published AQ600L specification; taper height keys per #2130).\n3. Goldens for the EDM test parts (square, 2-axis, taper) on the new dialect, and the dry-run kit refreshed for the owner.\n\nNot in scope: the `G0 Z0` start move (until the owner defines Z0); COND.DAT condition selection (#3183).\n\nDone means: the AQ600L machine posts the square, 2-axis and taper test parts with the LN2W dialect - taper as G51/G52 A + G50 with TP/TN - pinned by goldens; the Mark 21 dialect output is byte-identical; the dialect header still says NOT VERIFIED ON A CONTROL until the owner reports a clean dry run.\n\nRefs #1500, #2130, #617.\n",
